DESCRIPTION >
    Sessions: raw pageview rows over a caller-supplied range, for on-read
    session derivation (30-minute inactivity rule applied in JS, unchanged).
    Tenant-scoped; prunes via (site_id, timestamp), secondary sort by
    distinct_id matches the source's ORDER BY. Faithful 1:1 port of
    api/routes/sessions.js:29-45 (queryName 'sessions_pageviews'). Identity
    rule #19a: distinct_id is the row-grouping key downstream (canonical
    stitching key), no argMin/argMax in this query itself. Typed-column
    translation (SCOPE_v3.md §2.6): properties.site_id -> site_id, event ->
    event_type, properties.page_url -> page_url, properties.utm_source ->
    utm_source, properties.utm_medium -> utm_medium, properties.utm_campaign
    -> utm_campaign (all typed, Nullable per §2.6). No JSON-bag fields.
    Date range is REQUIRED here (the route 400s without both date_from/
    date_to) — ported as required params (date_from_ts/date_to_ts, full
    boundary strings), matching leads_count.pipe's naming but always-required
    per this source's actual validation.
    NOT YET PUSHED — validated read-only via `tb --cloud sql` only.
    DEPLOY FIX (tb --cloud deploy --check, ST_Staging v4.6.4): date/datetime
    params were declared String(param, required=True) then wrapped in
    toDateTime(...) — that combination failed with CANNOT_PARSE_DATETIME
    under --check's '__no_value__' placeholder injection (a non-date string
    toDateTime() can't parse). Fixed by declaring the param itself as
    DateTime(...) (matching the already-shipped Phase 4 pipes' proven
    pattern) and dropping the now-redundant toDateTime(...) wrapper — no
    SQL/filter logic changed, only the param type. Re-validated via
    tb --cloud sql with real values post-fix; parity held (see batch
    dispatch report).

NODE sessions_pageviews_node
SQL >
    %
    SELECT
        distinct_id,
        timestamp,
        page_url,
        utm_source,
        utm_medium,
        utm_campaign
    FROM events
    WHERE site_id = {{ String(site_id, required=True) }}
      -- $heartbeat is a ONE-SHOT page-exit beacon (tracker.js:432-436), admitted so
      -- deriveSessions can compute real dwell time: without it a single-page session
      -- ends on its only event and reports 0s (sessionization.js finalizeSession).
      -- SAFE because pageview_count is gated on '$pageview' at sessionization.js:69/:93
      -- (so bounce rate, pageviews-per-visitor, is unmoved) and the beacon carries NO
      -- utm_*/click IDs, so acquisitionKey() returns null and it cannot split a session.
      AND event_type IN ('$pageview', '$heartbeat')
      AND timestamp >= {{ DateTime(date_from_ts, required=True) }}
      AND timestamp < {{ DateTime(date_to_ts, required=True) }}
    ORDER BY distinct_id ASC, timestamp ASC
    LIMIT 50000

TYPE endpoint
